{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":23974317,"ns":0,"title":"André–Quillen cohomology","extract":"In commutative algebra and algebraic geometry, André–Quillen cohomology is a cohomology theory for commutative rings and their modules, constructed using the cotangent complex. It provides a derived generalization of the module of derivations and describes infinitesimal deformations, extensions, and obstructions of commutative algebras.","description":"Theory of cohomology for commutative rings","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}